3. Copying, Moving and Deleting Files
No.	Scenario-based interview task	Expected command

21	Copy file1 into file2.	cp file1 file2
22	Copy multiple files into a directory called Backup.	cp file1 file2 Backup/
23	Copy all files from Folder1 to Folder2.	cp Folder1/* Folder2/
24	Copy a complete directory with its contents.	cp -r Folder1 Folder2/
25	Move a file from one directory to another.	mv file1 DevOps/
26	Rename old.txt to new.txt.	mv old.txt new.txt
27	Delete all .log files in the current directory.	rm -f *.log
28	Delete files starting with the letter D.	rm -f D*
29	Copy data from one file to multiple files without overwriting existing content.	tee -a file2 file3
30	Create a backup copy of a file.	cp file1 file1.bak
